>rothes, leocrottas, mumaks, wumpuses, and mind flayers.

You can get additional information on some monsters directly within
the game.  Type '/' and then you can either specify a monster on the
screen, or you can type the name of the monster you want.  There
might not be information on All monsters, but I have heard of efforts
to make the data file more complete.

For further information, and possibly even pictures, you can always
refer to AD&D (Monster Manuals, Fiend Folios, etc).  There is a bit
of overlap, but not entirely.

By the way, I don't really know what a mimic looks like, since most
of the time it mimics chests, wands, scrolls, etc.  :)

